 +4, while D-sponsored polls show Constantino ahead", "Raters overwhelmingly call it Likely R despite the tight polling", "Constantino has out-raised Gendebien and holds a cash edge"], "rationale": "The district's R+10 lean and the Likely R consensus from nearly every rater anchor the forecast toward the Republican, but the polling average is nearly tied and the high-quality Siena poll shows Gendebien ahead, so the margin stays narrow. Prediction markets pricing Gendebien around 23% reinforce a Lean R outcome.", "watch": "Whether post-debate polling confirms the Siena result or reverts to the Republican-leaning average; another independent poll showing Gendebien ahead would move this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Elise Stefanik (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Elise Stefanik's retirement leaves this R+10 North Country seat open, and both parties are contesting it seriously. Anthony Constantino, a Republican with strong self-funded resources and a Trump endorsement, faces Democrat Blake Gendebien, who has run a well-funded campaign and made the DCCC's Red to Blue program. Recent polling is unusually split: a Times Union/Siena survey in early October put Gendebien up four points, while Democratic-sponsored polls from Impact Research and PPP show Constantino leading by three to five. Most professional raters still call the race Likely Republican, and prediction markets give the Democrat roughly a one-in-four chance. The fundamentals point Republican, but the polling keeps this closer than the district's lean alone would suggest.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1406, "margin": -6.22}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2036, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1958, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2007, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1538, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1549, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2301, "margin"